  "rationale": "structural: The requirement prescribes a public struct, builder signatures and trait impls, and the roots cover them.\n\n- **Struct:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#struct[OpenAiConfig]` declares `#[non_exhaustive] pub struct OpenAiConfig` with exactly the prescribed fields. These are `model`, `endpoint` and `api_key_env` as `Option<String>`, `api_key` as `Option<SecretString>`, and `options` as `BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>`.\n- **Trait impls:** the same struct derives `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `PartialEq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize`, which are the listed trait implementations.\n- **Builder methods:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#impl[OpenAiConfig]#1` has `new`, `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and `option`. Their signatures match the prescribed ones. `new` returns `Self::default()`. The setters take `self` by value, set the field, and return `Self`. `option` inserts into the map.\n\nThe other `OpenAiConfig` impl block, `impl[OpenAiConfig]#2`, holds the `resolved_*` helpers. These apply the defaults, which the agent configuration contract specifies, so they are not part of this requirement's structural obligations. Both supplied roots carry the `impl` markers, so no marker is missing.\n\nbehavioral: The reviewed tests cover every observable obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.OpenAiConfig`. I did not read the implementation source. I judged the tests against the requirement text alone.\n\n**Builders and fields**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` checks that `OpenAiConfig::new()` serializes to `{}`. It then applies `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and `option`, and asserts the full serialized form. A repeated option key overwrites the earlier value, and `options` holds both keys.\n- Because the builders produce exactly the expected JSON, each one sets only its own field.\n\n**Serde (`Serialize` and `Deserialize`)**\n- `all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials` deserializes an OpenAI config with `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key` and nested `options`. It asserts the JSON round-trips unchanged and that `PartialEq` holds after a string round-trip.\n- `openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults` deserializes `{\"backend\":\"openai\"}` and asserts it equals `AgentConfig::OpenAi(OpenAiConfig::new())`. That covers `Default`/`new` equivalence and `PartialEq`.\n\n**Defaults for omitted settings**\n- `option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic` asserts the default model is `gpt-6.1-sol` and the default endpoint is `https://api.openai.com/v1`.\n- The same test asserts the default options `max_output_tokens=16384` and `reasoning.effort=low`.\n- `openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults` checks that defaults fill only what is missing:\n  - A user-supplied `max_output_tokens` is kept.\n  - `reasoning` with only `summary` gains `effort`.\n  - A user-supplied `reasoning.effort` is kept.\n- `openai_uses_the_default_credential_variable` runs a child process with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set and asserts `OpenAiConfig::new().resolved_api_key()` returns it. That covers the default credential variable.\n\n**Overrides take effect**\n- A custom `api_key_env` that is absent produces an error naming that variable.\n- An explicit `api_key` is used over an absent env var, so it takes precedence.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` checks end to end that an overridden model (`local-test`), endpoint (local server) and API key are used in real requests.\n\n**`Clone` and `Debug`**\n- These are plain trait impls with no stated behavior beyond existence. The public-API export test `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers the type's presence in the public API inventory.\n- No independent observable obligation needs a further test.\n\nNo gap found.",
